<title>USA: S&amp;P MidCap 400 index gets two new companies.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P MidCap 400 index gets two new companies.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Equity Services Group of Standard &amp; Poor's said Friday it would replace Measurex Corp and Michael Foods Inc in the S&amp;P MidCap 400 Index with SunGard Data Systems Inc and Interstate Bakeries Corp at the close of trading on February 28.</p>
<p>SunGard and Interstate Bakeries are currently in the S&amp;P SmallCap 600.</p>
<p>Measurex is being acquired by Honeywell Inc, in the S&amp;P 500 category, while Michael Foods is merging with North Star Universal Inc, which is not in an S&amp;P index.</p>
<p>SunGard and Interstate Bakeries are to be replaced in the S&amp;P SmallCap 600 by CIBER Inc and Dialogic Corp.</p>
</text>
